    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside pairing of **Kyle Tucker** (80.39) and **Andy Pages** (74.15). Both benefit significantly from facing V\u00e1squez, who struggles with a 4.76 xERA, and the advantage of wind blowing out, which boosts their power profiles. **Jackson Merrill** (70.44) and **Cole Carrigg** (67.90) also present as elite options; **Jackson Merrill** specifically draws a favorable matchup against Sasaki, where a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher opens a window for him to exploit the stolen base category, our scarcest and most vital metric. **Sam Antonacci** (60.82) provides a high floor in the leadoff spot, bolstered by a strong platoon edge against Cecconi.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (42.90), who barely missed the cut. While his underlying metrics are solid, he is hampered by a daunting matchup against Miller, whose 2.42 xERA creates an aggressive SP Skill penalty that suppresses his overall efficiency score below our preferred threshold. We opted to prioritize the platoon advantages and favorable park factors found in our starting group. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL, and advise caution with **Josh Lowe** (43.94); despite his inclusion, his score is heavily pressured by Miller's dominance on the mound. Owners should keep a close eye on final lineup confirmations for any late-breaking weather alerts or defensive shifts that could impact **Liam Hicks** or **Drake Baldwin**.",
